<p>The leaked hashtable is not reported by LeakSanitizer, whereas it is rep=
orted by Valgrind. That's because glib2 specifically detects Valgrind and, =
in Valgrind's presence, turns off its custom memory allocator (<a href=3D"h=
ttps://developer.gnome.org/glib/stable/glib-Memory-Slices.html">g_slice</a>=
). One can force glib2 to be debugging-friendly even with LeakSanitizer, ho=
wever:</p>

